[statement]
A package installed for its condition never has, among its own
dependencies, a package holding a name a `!` entry of its condition
names, whatever version the entry admits: `e`'s condition is `base` and
`!docs`, `e` needs `docs`, and only `docs` answers it; apk does not
install `e`. The same holds for `!docs>1`, which `docs` 1 escapes.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:base

P:base
V:1

P:docs
V:1

P:e
V:1
D:docs
i:base !docs

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install base 1
install top 1
